# EXPECT-VIOLATION: mirash:WritableSignalShape
#
# R13b FAIL-CLOSED — a command signal declaring NO read_only capability at all.
#
# This fixture exists because the shape did NOT catch this before Phase 2. SHACL evaluates
# `sh:not [ sh:in (false) ]` per VALUE, so a signal with zero values passed vacuously: an
# undeclared command point read as safe. That is backwards for a capability flag — unknown
# writability is not permission. Phase 2 added `sh:minCount 1` so the missing case fails closed,
# matching the default-deny posture of .claude/rules/fieldbus-readonly.md.

@prefix mira: <https://ontology.factorylm.com/mira#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:   <https://example.org/fx#> .

ex:unknown_cmd a mira:CommandSignal .
